<p>German philosopher and social critic Jürgen Habermas died on Saturday in Starnberg, Germany, at 96, according to his publisher Suhrkamp. His work made him one of the world’s most influential philosophers and one of Germany’s leading public intellectuals.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/rSqUmetdn7BsBK1mpJi_4BC_WQeieYG47mHot3wkVFfN4HaM0rHByYBFHfdcDi5jVir_jgfLLi8AfTViaamgBTiyHP7giG-uoTfIk6zC_W8tzKaZWl9528gVM3npMNuafixV6iHeLpkpgPLW5UvAUItMDsmAJyzYzu4ufIi8mg' alt='Jürgen Habermas in a file photo.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Consensus-building: The Guardian and SCMP said Habermas was best known for a theory of political consensus-building centered on how public opinion forms in democracies.</li><li>Long intervention: SCMP said his public engagement stretched from critiques of fascist thought in the 1950s to later warnings about renewed militarism and nationalism in Germany.</li><li>European debates: The Guardian said he helped shape debate around European integration and the formation of the European Union.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>BBC News: BBC described Habermas as a rare philosopher whose ideas made him central to Germany’s public life after the war. (<a href='https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/crk8yxd2g0no'>BBC News</a>)</li><li>South China Morning Post: SCMP emphasized Habermas as the thinker who helped shape Germany’s post-war conscience at pivotal moments. (<a href='https://www.scmp.com/news/world/europe/article/3346630/jurgen-habermas-philosopher-who-shaped-germanys-post-war-conscience-dies-96'>South China Morning Post</a>)</li><li>The Guardian: The Guardian described him as a towering figure in the intellectual history of postwar Germany. (<a href='https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/mar/14/jurgen-habermas-german-philosopher-and-sociologist-dies-aged-96'>The Guardian</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/crk8yxd2g0no'>German philosopher and social critic Jürgen Habermas dies at 96</a> 